<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Twenty-three days of American and Israeli strikes have damaged eighty-one thousand homes across Iran, according to the Iranian Red Crescent, which says hospitals, schools, and ambulances have also been hit.</s> <s>The Red Crescent called the campaign a violation of international humanitarian law and demanded an emergency international response.</s> <s>No ceasefire is in sight, and President Trump has issued a forty-eight-hour ultimatum over the Strait of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hɔːrˈmuːz">Hormuz</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A drone struck <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɛl dɑːˈiːn">el-Daein</phoneme> Teaching Hospital on <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="iːd">Eid</phoneme>, killing sixty-four people in what the United Nations calls the world's largest humanitarian crisis.</s> <s>The World Health Organization has documented over two thousand deaths across two hundred thirteen attacks on healthcare facilities since Sudan's civil war began in April twenty twenty-three.</s> <s>Separately, military council chief <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈjæs.ər æl ˈæt.ɑː">Yasser al-Atta</phoneme> ordered all armed groups absorbed into the national army, a move that could unravel the twenty twenty <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdʒuː.bə">Juba</phoneme> Peace Agreement.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel's defense minister ordered Lebanese border villages leveled, using the words "like Gaza," to prevent one million displaced people from ever returning home.</s> <s>The military also plans to destroy <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kæsˈmiː.jə">Qasmiyeh</phoneme> Bridge near <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɔːr">Tyre</phoneme>, which would sever the city from the rest of the country.</s> <s>Systematic demolition of civilian villages is now stated policy along Israel's northern border.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Congo-Brazzaville, biometric voting devices sold as democratic infrastructure came pre-loaded with results, handing President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="dəˈniː sæˈsuː ŋˈɡɛs.oʊ">Denis Sassou-Nguesso</phoneme> nearly ninety-five percent of the vote.</s> <s>He has held power for forty of the last forty-seven years, making him one of the longest-ruling leaders on the African continent.</s> <s>Civil society group CAPGED has filed a legal challenge, though no court in the country's history has overturned a presidential election.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Uganda's main opposition leader <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈboʊ.bi waɪn">Bobi Wine</phoneme> fled the country and surfaced at the United States Capitol.</s> <s>Wine lost the twenty twenty-one presidential race to <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="joʊˈwɛr.i muːˈsɛv.ən.i">Yoweri Museveni</phoneme>, who has held power since nineteen eighty-six.</s> <s>He says he will meet American officials this week to seek pressure on <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="muːˈsɛv.ən.i">Museveni</phoneme> to allow his return.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers shot six Palestinians dead in the occupied West Bank in March alone, operating with de facto state protection under military occupation.</s> <s>Thirteen governments have demanded Israel prosecute the perpetrators, with several European capitals labeling the violence terrorism for the first time.</s> <s>Israeli authorities have not responded to any of the demands.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistani police beat activist <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæv.rə ˈbɑː.ri">Mavra Bari</phoneme> at a Women's Day march in Islamabad, then detained demonstrators under national security laws.</s> <s>Those laws let authorities jail protesters at independent gatherings while state-aligned events proceed without interference.</s> <s>Rights groups are demanding the release of all detainees, including lawyer <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="iːˈmɑːn məˈzɑː.ri">Imaan Mazari</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba suffered its second national blackout in a week as hospitals ran short of supplies restricted by the American embargo.</s> <s>Puerto Rican activists flew medicine to Havana in a gesture of Caribbean solidarity that bypassed official channels.</s> <s>Havana rejected a United States offer of diesel fuel conditioned on political concessions, leaving the power crisis unresolved.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India jailed thirty-three Bangladeshis, including children, for crossing the border, but the rights group Justice and Care says they were trafficking victims transported by paid brokers.</s> <s>The networks that moved them remain active, with no arrests on either side of the border.</s> <s>South Asia's anti-trafficking systems continue to punish victims while leaving recruiters untouched.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Hong Kong's ground-floor commercial rents have fallen below upper-floor rates for the first time, reversing decades of the city's commercial geography as businesses move down from once-cheap upper stories.</s> <s>Airspace closures from the Iran conflict and surging fuel surcharges have made long-haul flights unaffordable, pushing Easter travelers onto cross-border rail and selling out train tickets.</s> <s>Whether the city's travel industry recovers or contracts further now depends entirely on rail capacity and when the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hɔːrˈmuːz">Hormuz</phoneme> fighting ends.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesian President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="prɑːˈboʊ.woʊ suːbiˈɑːn.toʊ">Prabowo Subianto</phoneme> is targeting eight percent economic growth, a rate the country has not achieved since the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="suːˈhɑːr.toʊ">Suharto</phoneme> era.</s> <s>His plan rests on thirty thousand school kitchens, eighty thousand village cooperatives, and one million new homes to stimulate domestic demand.</s> <s>The government's own first-quarter projection is five and a half percent, and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="prɑːˈboʊ.woʊ">Prabowo</phoneme> has not explained how the programs close the gap.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Missiles have struck both <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="dɪˈmoʊ.nə">Dimona</phoneme> and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="næˈtænz">Natanz</phoneme>, two of the Middle East's most sensitive nuclear facilities.</s> <s>The International Atomic Energy Agency detected no abnormal radiation, but <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="næˈtænz">Natanz</phoneme> holds enriched uranium stockpiles that would contaminate the wider region if dispersed by a direct hit.</s> <s>WHO Director-General <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈtɛd.roʊs ɑːdəˈnɒm ɡɛˈbreɪ.ə.sʊs">Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus</phoneme> warned the conflict is edging toward a public health catastrophe without precedent.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Medicare's own chief has called TrumpRx narrow, undercutting the White House's promise of sweeping drug price relief.</s> <s>The program covers only cash-paying uninsured patients, leaving two hundred million insured Americans paying full price at the pharmacy counter.</s> <s>Unless Congress legislates the broader reform, the gap between presidential promise and actual policy will only widen.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Boston Dynamics' Atlas robot still cannot reliably grasp a small object, exposing the vast distance between humanoid spectacle and practical dexterity.</s> <s>The human hand's twenty-seven degrees of freedom depend on tactile feedback loops that no current sensor can replicate.</s> <s>Researchers say the breakthrough requires entirely new sensor architectures, not larger versions of what already exists.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A three hundred ninety-seven billion parameter artificial intelligence model now runs on a consumer Mac, a milestone that moves frontier AI from the cloud onto personal hardware.</s> <s>A technique called mixture-of-experts activates only four of five hundred twelve specialized networks per token, slashing memory requirements enough to fit two hundred nine gigabytes on a desktop machine.</s> <s>Once downloaded, the model cannot be censored, updated, or remotely revoked by its creators.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China's ASN-three-oh-one drone is built to hunt and destroy radar systems autonomously, giving Beijing a precision tool against air defense networks.</s> <s>Both the ASN and Iran's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʃɑːˈhɛd">Shahed</phoneme> trace their lineage to Israeli <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈhɑːr.pi">Harpy</phoneme> anti-radiation technology, but China engineered a radar killer while Iran optimized for cheap mass production.</s> <s>Nations that depend on radar-guided air defenses now face a threat those systems were never designed to counter.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>